{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/136757-adventure","id":136757,"title":"Adventure!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-14T08:19:54-07:00","id":136757,"title":"Adventure!","content":"Hello there fellow adventures, I recently acquired adventure and after reading it I have to say that I love it so much that I'm planning a game. However I'm sad that there is no more material for it I was wandering if there is any fan material available? specially new knacks?. Oh and one last thing, I have oberseved that the only advantage you get for ability mastery is an extra dice, all my players have told me that is worthless and i do agree to a certain point, I was thinking that maybe instead of an extra dice perhaps it permanently lowers the difficulty of the ability from 7 to 6, what do you think? Thanks for your help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T08:47:03-07:00","id":136774,"title":"","content":"There's a second edition of Adventure! coming, though it's far enough in the future that sticking with 1e for the moment is fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T08:49:03-07:00","id":136780,"title":"","content":"First. Welcome to Adventure!, you will NEVER leave! BWAHAHAHAHAHAHA!!! Ahem.<br /> Second, while the lack of expansion is sad on one hand, on the other A! stands on it's own so well that any expansion would just be gravy.<br /> Third, my group actually tried lowering target number to 6 and it got super crazy super fast. Ultimately we decided it was game-breakingly powerful. As a general rule I just let characters with mastery attempt things I wouldn't let non-master players try, and sometimes I lower their difficulties (number of successes needed). I also describe their actions with more flair and over the top narration.<br /> <br /> Hope that is helpful.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T10:42:10-07:00","id":136875,"title":"","content":"If you have access to Aberrant, one thing that I had my players do was treat your dot of Ability Mastery as a hyper-specialized Mega Attribute, for that ability only. You could roll that extra die separately for extra successes, or spend it to lower the difficulty for something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T10:43:56-07:00","id":136876,"title":"","content":"There's also this website I found, while running my Adventure! game: <a href=\"http://home.insightbb.com/~kinesys/aeon_adventure.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://home.insightbb.com/~kinesys/aeon_adventure.htm</a><br /> <br /> And a few knacks here, on a website that unfortunately only exists in memory: <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20110529215447/http://www.freewebs.com/blackjackal256/newknacks.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20110529...newknacks.html</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T19:20:10-07:00","id":137541,"title":"","content":"One thing I haven't read aberrant or trinity except for their wikipedia pages and the white wolf wiki so I'm a little bit ignorant. Wow thanks lustral I like what I see. I also like those advices about ability mastery but I have a suggestion, how about no botch? 1s have no longer any effect, yo cannot botch and they don't take away successes, what do you think? (next I will put a couple of personal knacks, I want to know if you consider them overpowered, thanks for your help) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T19:33:34-07:00","id":137581,"title":"","content":"I think a no botch rule would be a fine advantage. My group decided against the &quot;acts as mega-die&quot; plan that Lustral uses, but that's mostly because we did a fair amount of crossover stuff and we wanted Mega-dice to remain distinct.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T19:39:30-07:00","id":137613,"title":"","content":"Interesting! We used our rule for exactly the same reason -- not because we wanted Mega-dice to remain distinct, but because we had significant crossover planned for the future (Adventure! into Aberrant, then Aberrant into Trinity) and wanted the &quot;lesser&quot; Inspired to still remain somewhat capable, if only in their very narrow fields of specialty.<br /> <br /> But yes, that botch-protection rule sounds very worthwhile. Also, keep in mind that in the Aeonverse games, 1s <i>do not</i> subtract from successes like in World of Darkness <i>by default</i>. You only bother with 1s if you have not rolled any successes to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T19:42:59-07:00","id":137626,"title":"","content":"Also, (one of my players just reminded me) we always allow 10's to explode on mastery rolls.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T19:45:43-07:00","id":137631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/136757-adventure?p=137626#post137626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, (one of my players just reminded me) we always allow 10's to explode on mastery rolls.<br /> <br /> -Slag</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless of Attribute qualities? Nice. Makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:18:14-07:00","id":138128,"title":"","content":"hum...10 explode all the time...nice but how about something like this, once during every session you get to chose one of these options regarding your mastered ability: turn a botch into a regular failure, turn a regular failure into regular success, turn a regular success into an exceptional success. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T11:51:52-07:00","id":138305,"title":"","content":"The botch -&gt; failure, failure -&gt; success thing could work, but there aren't really hard and fast grades of success in the system Adventure! uses. For example, in NWoD, getting between 1 and 4 success is rated a &quot;success&quot;, and getting 5 or more is an &quot;exceptional success&quot;. That system doesn't exist for Adventure!. The Storyteller is encouraged to have better results for more successes, but that's mostly a storytelling element and not a mechanical one.<br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind that in Adventure!, 10s <i>do not</i> explode all the time. That's a bonus given for the right circumstances; usually, one does not receive any exploding dice. When you have 4 or more dots in an Attribute, the character picks up a <i>quality</i> associated with that Attribute (essentially an adjective, or a one- or two-word phrase describing what that character specializes in). For example, I'd have a character with Dexterity 4 (Quick Reflexes). If I normally roll a Dexterity-based dice pool, I do not reroll 10s -- but if that Dexterity-based roll is the result of an action where having &quot;quick reflexes&quot; is a good bonus, then I am allowed to reroll those 10s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2464,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","user":"lustral_star","date":". 05-15-2014, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T14:43:05-07:00","id":138411,"title":"","content":"There were a few more ideas for what to do with Ability Masteries from the Aberrant 2.0 wiki, when discussing Paramorphs. They had some very interesting mechanics for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T17:16:29-07:00","id":138658,"title":"","content":"I guess that it's just that I believe that mastery in one ability should be something more cooler than just one more dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T19:49:31-07:00","id":138745,"title":"","content":"I like the option of being able to spend a point of Inspiration to reroll all of the failed dice in a pool that includes an Ability Mastery. Beyond that, I prefer to represent \u201chypercompetence\u201d through Heroic Knacks rather than Ability Mastery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/136757-adventure?p=138411#post138411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were a few more ideas for what to do with Ability Masteries from the Aberrant 2.0 wiki, when discussing Paramorphs. They had some very interesting mechanics for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not particularly fond of saying that daredevils are paramorphs; but I <i>do</i> rather like most of the paramorphs stuff on that site despite that. For ease of reference, <a href=\"http://swiki.fancruft.com/index.php?title=Aberrant_2.0_Paramorphs\" target=\"_blank\">here\u2019s what we\u2019re talking about</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-15-2014, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T11:41:21-07:00","id":139607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/136757-adventure?p=138745#post138745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not particularly fond of saying that daredevils are paramorphs; but I <i>do</i> rather like most of the paramorphs stuff on that site despite that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we can agree to disagree -- Golden Rule <i>and all that jazz!</i> *jazz hands* Most of my advice comes from the game that I ran/run, which sets Daredevils, Mesmerists, and Stalwarts on one level with Paramorphs, Psiads, and Novas on another level. I draw distinctions between Daredevils/Paramorphs (which is normal), but also between Mesmerists/Psiads and Stalwarts/Novas (which is not what the game developers <i>intended</i>, per se). Having said that, yes, they really did a bang-up job writing some material for Paramorphs on that wiki. Firanai could probably get a lot of mileage out of repurposing some of that material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T11:43:10-07:00","id":139609,"title":"","content":"In fact, if the power level of those Knacks are toned down, some of them could be very useful Daredevil Knacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T11:13:04-07:00","id":140744,"title":"","content":"I'm already using that material, thanks all of you for the help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. By the way I have a question, what happened to the inspired during the time period from 1940 to 1998? did they hide? did they die? did they retire? did they participate in the world war?. I'm asking because I'm planning a campaign in which the players jump to several places in the timeline, 1924, 1934, 1944, 1954, 1964 and 1974. I have found very little information and I would like to know if there is more, for my part I have created this background, tell me what you think.<br /> As tensions raised between the different countries and the winds of war were blowing again the different governments of the world started to pay more attention to the strange stories about the inspired. Before they dismissed them as nothing more than ridiculous and exaggerated tales destined to help sell more papers and to entertain the masses with their bizarre and bombastic adventures.<br /> However as their research about them kept going on it showed that these individuals were very real and had indeed powers and capabilities beyond human, so they started to see them as something different: weapons. The different nations formed secret agencies with the objective to capture and use these individuals by whatever means necessary and if they didn't comply....well...the agents had to make sure that the other side didn't get them. The most compassionate would help them live under government surveillance, the most ruthless would murder them. The Aeon society did the best it could to stop the proliferation of these superhuman weapons and superscience weaponry but despite their best efforts it continued.<br /> These secret agencies fought against each other during the war in order to give their side and edge, taking into account the scale of what was at stake in their battles their conflict became a third front on it's own right. The devastation and damage that these super-individuals brought to the war was mind-blowing, the powers that be became terrified and impressed, reinforcing their belief that these individuals should be contained or eliminated. Seeing the horror of the war was the last straw for Doctor primoris who had grown more and more disappointed with humanity. He decided to take the matters into his own hands, he would enforce peace even if that meant conquering the world and ruling as a dictator. Luckily the Aeon society stopped him in time but not without a great cost to their members, after his defeat he disappeared never to be seen again.<br /> After the war the soviet union and the united states redoubled their efforts to capture or eliminate the inspired using the chaos of a devastated world and the paranoia of the 50's. Before they were shown some mercy if they agreed to live quiet lives but seeing how powerful they were that option became invalid, they were simply to dangerous and useful to let them run free. In the process they made sure to erase all evidence of their existence from the public to guarantee that none but themselves could use them. The rest of inspired and secret organizations went into hiding in an effort to avoid persecution, some of them would still act from the shadows and others would simply retire.<br /> Maxwell banished in order to help the inspired disappear so they wouldn't end as pawns in the cold war, at least that was the initial plan. As time passed he expanded his operations as much as he could with the help of the of the now secret aeon society and established a sanctuary network to protect the inspired from the world and the world from the inspired. But no matter how much they hid, they kept coming after them. The more time it passed the more he understood that as long as there were greedy governments and organizations bent on exploiting their power the world and the inspired would never be safe.<br /> The situation went bad with the Korean war, grew desperate with the close call of the Cuban missile crisis and went further down to the breaking point with the Vietnam war.The public never knew the horrors and battles between inspired and their creations that took place in those dark days. Under the orders of both the soviet union and the united states the inspired fought, died and designed more and more horrible weapons in a frantic race to outmatch the other side. It was only thanks to the intervention of maxwell, the aeon society and even doctor primoris in one occasion that the world wasn't destroyed. (both the 50s, 60s and 70s adventure becomes more like a James bond and espionage type of roleplaying game)<br /> Maxwell decided that there was only one option to end the madness, he was very reticent to intervene in such a direct way but he saw no other exit. Maxwell with the help of the Aeon society and other inspired, both friends and foes alike, planned and directed an all assault all over the globe that destroyed the government agencies that enslaved the inspired. At the same time they further erased any evidence of their existence from even the most secret vaults. They even erased the memories from several key members in the governments. Last but not least and with great pain they also removed the inspired that didn't agree with the secrecy. By the end of the 70s no one ever knew that the inspired ever existed, humanity would be free to pursue it's own path and the inspired could finally rest in peace...at least till 1998. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 05-18-2014, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T11:25:48-07:00","id":140748,"title":"","content":"Interesting background -- and perhaps more interesting than the &quot;official&quot; story, if you're going to have the players be active during those years.<br /> <br /> After World War II, the shock of The Bomb shattered what little Hope remained from the Adventure! age. Those Inspired who were not dead slunk off to the shadows, tails between their legs. The Aeon Society worked in secret, cataloging unusual activity around the world, and working to keep it out of the public eye. Specific members of the Inspired -- those named NPCs from Adventure! -- either remained with Aeon, or retired to lives of relative normalcy. There were reports of a small upsurge in Inspired activity during the 70s, I believe, though it was a single throwaway comment and no details were ever mentioned regarding it.<br /> <br /> For the most part, things were pretty boring for the Inspired between 1945 and 1998.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T16:28:53-07:00","id":141010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/136757-adventure?p=139607#post139607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we can agree to disagree -- Golden Rule <i>and all that jazz!</i> *jazz hands* Most of my advice comes from the game that I ran/run, which sets Daredevils, Mesmerists, and Stalwarts on one level with Paramorphs, Psiads, and Novas on another level. I draw distinctions between Daredevils/Paramorphs (which is normal), but also between Mesmerists/Psiads and Stalwarts/Novas (which is not what the game developers <i>intended</i>, per se). Having said that, yes, they really did a bang-up job writing some material for Paramorphs on that wiki. Firanai could probably get a lot of mileage out of repurposing some of that material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also draw a distinction between stalwarts and novas, though it\u2019s a distinction of degree rather than of kind: as I see it, Stalwarts are what <b>Aberrant</b> calls Stealth Novas: their Dynamic Knacks always take the form of attribute boosts of one sort or another; and in terms of sheer power, they\u2019re much more subdued than the typical Mega-Attributes of <b>Aberrant</b>. All other differences stem from <b>Adventure!</b>\u2019s more streamlined game mechanics and are not actual differences.<br /> <br /> I generally <i>don\u2019t</i> draw a distinction between mesmerists and psiads: any differences that seem to exist between them are strictly the result of <b>Adventure!</b>\u2019s more streamlined game mechanics. I <i>do</i> draw a distinction between psiads and psions, though.<br /> <br /> One thing I\u2019m hoping to see from the upcoming Trinity Continuum is a consistency in the rules that renders the above difference of opinion moot, whether it be a clearly expressed vision of just what the relationship between Talents and Max Mercer is (if any) or an overall framework for exotic abilities that is consistently applied across all of the individual eras and eliminates the cognitive dissonance of using different rules to model what it conceptually minor variations of the same thing. <br /> <br /> And as will probably come as no surprise, I draw a strong distinction between daredevils and paramorphs: to me, they\u2019re not even the same kind of thing, with daredevils being baseline humans who demonstrate just how much baselines are capable of, whereas paramorphs (which arguably ought to be singular, as only one is known to exist) are time manipulators and travelers. What I like about the Aberrant 2.0 wiki\u2019s paramorphs is that <i>if</i> you\u2019re going to equate daredevils to paramorphs, that is how I would do it. I especially like how the Time Powers tend to evoke over-the-top action hero tropes such as \u201cbullet time\u201d.<br /> <br /> I tend to think, though, that Time Powers ought to come with some sort of Paradox mechanic that risks messing up the paramorph if he doesn\u2019t apply some restraint in using them. The simplest mechanic for this would be to say that each time a paramorph uses Temporal Manipulation, the Storyteller gains the right to use one instance of Dramatic Editing against them when he feels it\u2019s appropriate to do so: low-level Temporal Powers trigger Minor Onscreen Effects, mid-level Temporal Powers trigger Major Onscreen Effects, and high-level Temporal Powers trigger Obvious Continuity Violations. A paramorph can downgrade a Paradox by one step by asking for an immediate Complication, and can negate a Paradox at any time by paying the Inspiration for an equivalent Dramatic Edit; conversely, the Storyteller can intensify a Paradox by one step by introducing a Plot Ramification. I would have this Paradox system <i>replace</i> the usual Inspiration cost for Temporal Manipulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-17-2014, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T18:14:22-07:00","id":141090,"title":"","content":"Paradox complications? That sounds fun. Unfortunately I'm out and about, so reading your post in detail is difficult, but a cursory glance reminds me of the issues a Changeling risks for talecrafting or fateweaving or whatever it's called in C:tL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T18:21:49-07:00","id":141096,"title":"","content":"Yeah; the specifics are different, but the basic principle is similar: you try to direct the flow of time (<b>Aberrant</b>) or fate (<b>Changeling</b>) and it will resist the changes and/or spawn unintended consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T06:28:23-07:00","id":141502,"title":"","content":"Correct if I'm wrong since I haven't read much but for what I have gathered if we were explaining the differences between novas, psions and paramorphs in mage terms could it be something like this?:<br /> <br /> Paramorphs, sphere domains: Entropy, Time, Correspondence.<br /> Novas, sphere domains: Life, Matter, Forces.<br /> Psions, sphere domains: Mind, Prime, Spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T13:59:39-07:00","id":141776,"title":"","content":"Psions don\u2019t have much of anything that would translate to Prime or Spirit, unless you consider noetic energy to be analogous to Prime; they <i>do</i>, however, include three broadly-defined types, one of which could be modeled (very roughly) using Mind and Correspondence, one of which would fall primarily under Forces, and the third of which would be covered by Life. <br /> <br /> Novas do deal primarily in Forces, Life, and Matter; but they deal with Prime (in the form of Quantum) to the same extent that psions do. As well, there are Quantum Powers suitable for every Sphere that has a presence in the setting, including mental manipulation and time travel. Personally, I think a better way to characterize them in Mage terms is that they show a strong preference for Vulgar effects. With a few exceptions, they don\u2019t do subtle. <br /> <br /> For Paramorphs, it depends on which theory you buy into. I always get them mixed up, so apologies in advance if I did so again: Andrew Bates\u2019 theory is that there\u2019s one paramorph (Max Mercer), whose abilities would fall under the purview of Time. Bruce Baugh\u2019s theory is that daredevils are paramorphs, and that their powers are primarily what <b>Mage</b> would call Entropy, followed up by Time and a smattering of everything else; but much like Novas are better off described as specializing in Vulgar effects, Baugh-style paramorphs excel at Coincidental effects \u2014 almost exclusively so. <br /> <br /> All that said, it probably goes without saying that describing the difference between the three types of Morphs in Mage terms is going to be about as relevant as describing, say, Vampire Disciplines, Werewolf Gifts, Wraith Arcanoi, and Changeling Arts in Mage terms. That is, it\u2019s better to consider them on their own terms rather than looking at them through the lens of Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T07:12:27-07:00","id":143405,"title":"","content":"I pretty much use the 2.0 rules for Paramorphs exclusively, even for Adventure! era Daredevils (though they start with much less in the way of Transformation Points). It's been much more satisfying for us to just go 'they're more than baseline humans', because baseline humans being able to stand up to the quantum gods in our game violates suspension of disbelief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T22:21:26-07:00","id":144177,"title":"","content":"So, I decided to actually sit down and read through the Trinity pdfs I have in my White Wolf folder on my computer, starting with Adventure! because it was just one book and the first in the timeline.<br /> <br /> So I'm reading along, digging the two-fisted pulp goodness, when I spotted this little entry: &quot;As famed explorer, <u>Henry Jones Jr.</u>, asserts...&quot;<br /> <br /> The bright spark I feel in my soul is a feeling I recognize well: when I am well and truly a fan of something new. If this is truly a shout-out to what I think it is, then this gameline deserves all the very best it can be given.<br /> <br /> I now await the new editions of Trinity with the same anticipation as I do EX3. God bless America! /salute","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T22:56:20-07:00","id":144202,"title":"","content":"Ah, I love Sarah Gettel's writings. Lots of fun people in Adventure!, real AND imagined. It's not anywhere in the setting material, but there was an expedition to Antarctica/the South Pole in 1928 by Admiral Byrd -- to whom I am related. I've even got a recording of his expedition and interviews he conducted (and boy can you tell people back then didn't know how to talk while being filmed!)<br /> <br /> Long story short, my players went with him on his expedition to Antarctica and found a realm of dinosaurs buried under the polar ice -- a &quot;Land That Time Didn't Remember&quot;, as they named it. Of course, all footage of the dinosaurs was lost during their daring escape from members of the Society of Thule after foiling their plans to use dinosaurs to create an army -- but they DID turn Admiral Byrd's wrecked plane into a snow sled / hovercraft.<br /> <br /> They also knocked out an allosaurus with a shovel to its face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2464,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","user":"lustral_star","date":". 05-21-2014, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T23:36:13-07:00","id":144222,"title":"","content":"<b><i><a href=\"http://www.marx-brothers.org/whyaduck/info/movies/scenes/secofwar.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Duck Soup</a>:<br /> <br /> Firefly:</i></b> Have you got a license?<br /> <b><i>Chicolini:</i></b> License? No, butta my dog, he's gotta millions of 'em. Believe me, he's some smart dog. You know he went with Admiral Byrd to the Pole?<br /> <b><i>Firefly:</i></b> I'll bet the dog got to the Pole first.<br /> <b><i>Chicolini:</i></b> You win.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I kid, I kid. I wish I was related to a famous explorer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T09:12:17-07:00","id":144522,"title":"","content":"Hello there fellow adventures I wanted your advice on something. My players have asked me if they can include these backgrounds and I wanted to know your opinion about them, not only in terms of system but also if you think that they fit within the setting. Thanks for your help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Patron.<br /> <i>Jacob was surrounded by the corrupt police force, their boss was approaching with a mocking expression in his face, ready to beat and rob him &quot;My boss will want to talk to you but first let's have a little fun&quot;. Jacob pulled one card from his pocket and offered it to him, the dirty cop was confused by his act but he took it and inspected it. All color disappeared from his face and now it was Jacob the one with the mocking expression. &quot;Well after this I think my boss would like a talk with you too&quot;</i><br /> <br /> A patron is a powerful individual that sponsors the player character. Wether a great artist, a stage magician, a brave explorer or a genius scientist, through his actions or his creations, the player has attracted the attention of someone with considerable means. This person can be a playboy millionaire, a crime boss, a religious figure or a complete mystery. His motives are equally varied, perhaps he wants to commission one painting, a machine for a very odd task, search for a lost civilization in the African jungle or maybe he just wants his company. The support that the player receives comes in the form of money, contacts and influence. The patron may get the player out of jail, get him invitations to exclusive parties or provide money for his projects. It's important to understand that although having the backing of someone powerful and wealthy has some juicy advantages it also has it's drawbacks. First of all the player is an investment and from time to time his patron will expect some revenue in the form of a new artistic piece, a new invention or a new discovery. Also rich people love to boast about their possessions and like a prized stallion the player can be expected to attend parties where his patron can show him to his friends. Last but not least reputation is as precious as money for these people and pride runs high in them. If the player embarrasses or abuses his patrons trust he can find himself punished in the best of cases or with no more patron in the worst, perhaps even making their previous patron into an enemy! They must understand what their patron wants and what is his reputation if they want to avoid trouble. The number of dots indicates just how powerful his patron is, one dot represents an individual with just a little bit more means that the player while with five dots it's one of the wealthiest and most connected persons in the country. In the enhanced version of this background the player character has someone truly legendary as his patron. It can be a criminal mastermind like the ubiquitous dragon, an exceptional wealthy individual like Maxwell, the mysterious old man from the IDA or the secret leader of branch 9. Having someone like this as a patron opens a box of almost unlimited resources to the player but it will also make him the target of very dangerous individuals and the expectations put on him by his patron can be soul crushing. In system terms the patron of the player character has the backgrounds influence, contacts and resources at the same level as the players background in patron. The patron can give a number of favors per week equal to the rating in the patron background. Finally the player has a lifestyle equal to the resources of his patron minus 1.<br /> <br /> -Telluric fountain.<br /> <i>Gaspar was exhausted, in his state he didn't had the energy to even light a match. However he was quickly approaching his secret refuge, once he made sure for the twelve time that nobody was following him he entered the cave. He could already feel it as it got closer, the warm of the light was bathing him when he reached the opening. There he gorged himself in the divine energy, he was ready for whatever fate wanted to throw at him.</i><br /> <br /> A telluric fountain is a place filled with special crystals that store and irradiate telluric energy which the player has access. It's assumed that the player character is the only one who knows where is it and how to access it (for now). Nevertheless this is not an easy background to have despite it's usefulness. Unless the player has resources, followers and other backgrounds to protect and hide the fountain he's going to have a very difficult time keeping it. With the right instruments telluric energy is easily detectable and there are a significant number of very powerful individuals and organizations looking for telluric crystals. If by any chance they learn of the players character stash they would stop at nothing to steal it from him, something that can make his life very miserable in many ways. In system terms a telluric fountain generates a number of inspiration points per day equal to it's rating in the background and has a capacity for storage equal to (5 x rating). In it's enhanced version the player character has hit the motherload! The fountain generates 10 points per day and can storage up to 50 points. BUT if anybody ever finds it..... well...let's just say that the player character is going to need a whole army of veteran soldiers equipped with the best gear and a fortress with walls made of steel just to fend off the first wave of enemies.<br /> <br /> -Retainer. <br /> <i>Miss Genevieve was tied to a chair inside a bar with no way out and with several goons ready to take her away. &quot;Nobody is coming for you sweetheart, better for you to get comfortable with our company&quot;. The goons hadn't noticed the click in Miss Genevieve ring as she pressed it. &quot;I beg to differ sir. If I may I would like to present you to my bodyguard Mustafah&quot;, &quot;oh really? and where is he?&quot; As he finished his sentence one of the walls exploded, taking with it several goons, a giant figure with a fez and a white suit entered and started to beat the hell out of anybody who was still standing till everyone was on the floor unconscious or moaning in pain. &quot;Madam I hope I'm not to late?&quot; &quot;No, mustafah you arrived just in time&quot;</i><br /> <br /> A retainer is a highly skilled person at the service of the Player. The relationship between the two, the way in which he pays for him/her and what her skill set is depends on the player. He can be trusted friend or just a professional relation. He can be a strong bodyguard or a sneaky thief. The player can remunerate them in various ways like money, contacts or with other more..esoteric means. The retainer although competent can never outsmart or steal the light from the player, except if it's relevant to the story or has an ability that the player has not. He is loyal to the player character and has his best interests in mind but he will tolerate no bad treatment or foolish risks that endanger both of their lives. Although respectful he has enough trust with the player to be honest and blunt with him when he needs to be. Despite all of this the retainer is still a human being and like that is susceptible to blackmail, intimidation and torture and no matter how skillful he is, sometimes he commits mistakes like everyone else. If the player character uses him to much or puts him in danger to often he could find himself with a cadaver in his consciousness, the retainer is there to help but his well being is also the players responsibility. The number of dots indicates just how useful or competent he is, a retainer with one dot is the typical child sidekick that helps more thanks to sheer luck than skill while with 5 dots the player has the equivalent of batman's butler Alfred. In system terms the player creates another character just like the one described in the creation process, minus the inspired part. For each dot in the background the player has 10 extra points of experience to spend on him. The 5 dot gives the right to turn the servant into an inspired in which case the creation process follows the original path and the experience bonuses are cut in half.<br /> <br /> -Spies.<br /> <i>Mister Garrinton was calmly sitting in his nemesis office, while his Mobster lackey was boasting about his plan to ruin him. &quot;Are you finish?&quot; &quot;What?!&quot; &quot;I'm asking if you have finished, this is growing tedious&quot; &quot;why you little piece of..&quot; &quot;Stop there, let's see what I have here, I think you may find it interesting&quot; He pulled one file from his briefcase and opened it. &quot;Hum...interesting that you would choose that side of the port for the contraband and oh! look at this? you have Judge Carver in your pocket. By the way I think the way you murdered that poor girl Clarice was way to messy....&quot; The mobster had a terrified expression in his face &quot; How did you?...&quot; &quot;Silence!&quot; Garrinton raised from his chair and smashed his fists in the table, leaving a mark. &quot;This is only the tip of what I have on you and believe me it can get much much worse. Now sit down and let's talk about how are you gonna help me get to your boss...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Spies represent a highly specialized type of follower or contact, in certain ways they are far more useful but there are also more dangers. Spies are agents at the service of the player that can provide several services related to illegal or secret activities. This includes: access to classified information, planting false information, stealing, assassination, kidnapping, shadowing, smuggling and many more. Each agent reports directly to the player and no one else and has in his charge a small squad of men. The spies can never complete a mission in which the player is participating, they can only help by making it easier. An example would be that the spies of one of the players Kidnap the daughter of the ambassador an while he goes to pay the fee, the players have time to search through his documents in his hotel room. Another one would be that the player sends his assassins to assault the building distracting the goons while they enter using the back door. There are several risks with spies, they are professional but again they are also human. Due to the nature of their operations they are susceptible to be captured, bribed or even killed and if one operation goes wrong it can have some serious repercussions for the player. One of his agents could get captured and interrogated giving away the players implication, retaliation would sure follow. In the enhanced version of this background the player character has his own secret agency which makes him the terror of the underworld but it also escalates the danger to himself and his agents significantly. In system terms the player character can order one operation per dot and per week although the time can change depending on the difficulty of the task. The player has to roll his background dots but before he rolls Intelligence + command and adds its successes as extra dice to the main roll. The difficulty and the consequences for failure are set by the game master. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T09:52:06-07:00","id":144542,"title":"","content":"Both Patron and Retainer would be very appropriate for a pulp setting in general. Spies could be appropriate, depending on how you want to run your game -- however, it seems (to me, at least) to be something appropriate for a game in the 1940's, 50's, 60's, and 70's. Telluric Fountain... while I can't really imagine those don't exist <i>in some form</i> (those crystals do grow in places, after all), it seems like it might violate some of the foundations of the game (Inspiration is difficult for the characters to regain in large amounts). The game tends to focus on rewarding Inspiration for a character's actions, not being in a specific place or having access to certain materials. That one ultimately comes down to how you want to run your game, and how you want your game to play out. If you include that, be prepared for players to be throwing around fireballs and Dramatic Edits all day long. Inspiration and Telluric Energy will become a <i>muc</i><i>h</i> more devalued resource.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T14:18:38-07:00","id":144848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/136757-adventure?p=144177#post144177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I decided to actually sit down and read through the Trinity pdfs I have in my White Wolf folder on my computer, starting with Adventure! because it was just one book and the first in the timeline.<br /> <br /> So I'm reading along, digging the two-fisted pulp goodness, when I spotted this little entry: &quot;As famed explorer, <u>Henry Jones Jr.</u>, asserts...&quot;<br /> <br /> The bright spark I feel in my soul is a feeling I recognize well: when I am well and truly a fan of something new. If this is truly a shout-out to what I think it is, then this gameline deserves all the very best it can be given.<br /> <br /> I now await the new editions of Trinity with the same anticipation as I do EX3. God bless America! /salute</div> </div> </div> </div>The original advertisement for Adventure! which was done up to look like a newspaper also had a side story listed on <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lamont_Cranston\" target=\"_blank\">Lamont Cranston</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T17:35:06-07:00","id":145015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/136757-adventure?p=144848#post144848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The original advertisement for Adventure! which was done up to look like a newspaper also had a side story listed on <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lamont_Cranston\" target=\"_blank\">Lamont Cranston</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mwahahaha, <b>Mwahahaha</b>, <b>HAAAHAHAHAHAHAHA</b>! /evil cackle<br /> <br /> <i>Who knows what evil lurks in the hearts of men?</i><br /> <br /> <i>The</i> <b><i>Mesmerist</i></b> <i>knows...</i> *Cracka-BOOM!*<br /> <br /> (Love the Shadow movie! Need to watch it again...)<br /> <br /> (By the way, where is this ad? I'd love to see it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T21:12:12-07:00","id":145262,"title":"","content":"First appeared in the back of Aberrant. Page 278-ish.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/7ZxMzu4.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/7ZxMzu4l.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T21:15:05-07:00","id":145263,"title":"","content":"So many memories... And every single one of them a wonderful memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T04:32:32-07:00","id":145515,"title":"","content":"Great tagline, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2959-bates","name":"Bates","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2959_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T09:20:23-07:00","id":145734,"title":"","content":"In the reboot that they are making, the trinity continuum main book is going to contain a general description and timeline of the setting? or is it just going to be the rules and then each era is going to be a supplement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T12:30:32-07:00","id":145917,"title":"","content":"Each era is going to be a supplement; but the core book is <i>also</i> going to feature an \u201cera\u201d of its own: a modern-day action/adventure setting featuring Talents. So you\u2019ll be able to run something in the Trinity Continuum straight out of the box, as it were, even without supplements such as \u00c6on, Aberrant, or Adventure!. (As well, those three aren\u2019t going to be the only era supplements; though we haven\u2019t been told what other eras will be featured; just that Ian has several lined up.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T13:14:13-07:00","id":145965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/136757-adventure?p=145917#post145917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each era is going to be a supplement; but the core book is <i>also</i> going to feature an \u201cera\u201d of its own: a modern-day action/adventure setting featuring Talents. So you\u2019ll be able to run something in the Trinity Continuum straight out of the box, as it were, even without supplements such as \u00c6on, Aberrant, or Adventure!. (As well, those three aren\u2019t going to be the only era supplements; though we haven\u2019t been told what other eras will be featured; just that Ian has several lined up.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Although \u00c6on, Aberrant, and Adventure! remain the primary, 'tentpole', eras - there's a reason 'Trinity' is still in the title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T09:27:00-07:00","id":147881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/136757-adventure#post136757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh and one last thing, I have oberseved that the only advantage you get for ability mastery is an extra dice, all my players have told me that is worthless and i do agree to a certain point, I was thinking that maybe instead of an extra dice perhaps it permanently lowers the difficulty of the ability from 7 to 6, what do you think? Thanks for your help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one way that i got around this problem - and that worked wonderfully for the Adventure game i STed - was to &quot;spread the love&quot; by allowing inovations and inventions to apply to ability mastery <b>in all skills</b>, instead of just the scientific/technical ones, allowing for things like mind-controlling/death-dealing harmonics/music (Perform), revolutionary diet-exercise problems that make unaging supersoldiers out of weaklings (Endurance/Might), wall-shattering fighting moves (brawl, martial arts) and other deliciously pulpy stuff with only minor tweaks at most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T18:12:58-07:00","id":148299,"title":"","content":"So if I understand correctly you gave them a free knack int the ability they mastered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T18:55:09-07:00","id":148320,"title":"","content":"I think he's referring to Innovations and Inventions -- letting people with Ability Mastery develop some kind of super-science device associated with their Mastered ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T04:58:06-07:00","id":148600,"title":"","content":"Hum......now thats an interesting idea, ill ask my players and see what they think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T03:23:32-07:00","id":149289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/136757-adventure?p=148320#post148320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he's referring to Innovations and Inventions -- letting people with Ability Mastery develop some kind of super-science device associated with their Mastered ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly that, though by the line of thought i used an incredibly unique and complex to develop violin or musical score sheet could be as valid as a &quot;device&quot; as some crazy vehicle or rocket-pack.<br /> <br /> Such &quot;informal inventors&quot; worked pretty well to further reinforce the pulp/golden age element of Adventure. We even made some allowance for the occasional uninspired antagonist/acquitance possessing a skill or background at 6 and the results were fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-26-2014, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}